course: dictionary
lesson: 8233
title: Revolt: rising up or feeling sick
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A revolt is when many people rise up against the people in charge, such as rulers or kings. «In 1381 English peasants angry about taxes and unfair laws marched on London in the Peasants' Revolt.» The clues are angry, unfair laws and marched on London: the people were fighting back against those in power.
explain: Revolt can be a noun (a revolt) or a verb (to revolt). «Boudica, queen of the Iceni, led a big revolt after the Romans treated her people badly.» Here revolt is a noun, a rising against rulers. Ask yourself: is the sentence about people in power, or about something disgusting?
explain: Revolt has a second, very different meaning. «The smell from the bins was revolting.» Revolting means really disgusting, and to be revolted by something is to feel sick about it. Swap in disgusting: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: A revolt is a fight or protest by many people against their rulers or the people in charge.
fact: Revolt can be a noun («a revolt») or a verb («to revolt», «revolted», «revolting»).
fact: «The Peasants' Revolt» happened in England in 1381, when peasants protested against angry taxes and unfair laws.
fact: Boudica led a revolt in Britain against the Romans, who had treated her family and people badly.
fact: Informal: «revolting» means really disgusting, and «revolted by» means feeling sick about something.
exercise: «Enslaved people resisted in many ways, from revolts on ships to running away.» What is a revolt? | *A fight or protest against people in power | A kind of boat | A long holiday on a ship | A way of cooking food
exercise: «The smell from the bins was revolting.» What does revolting mean here? | Very kind | *Really disgusting | Rising up against a king | Very quiet
exercise: Find the word that means a rising against rulers in: «Boudica led a big revolt after the Romans treated her people badly.» | Romans | people | *revolt | led
test: «The Zhou dynasty taught that disasters and revolts show a ruler has lost the right to rule.» In this sentence, what are revolts? | Long journeys across the sea | Parties held by the ruler | *Rebellions against a ruler who has lost the right to rule | Kind gifts to the people
test: Mia was revolted by the rotten fish. What does revolted mean? | Sleepy | Excited | Quiet | *Disgusted
exam: In «The peasants began to revolt against unfair taxes», what does revolt mean? | *To refuse to obey and rise up | A long walk | To make someone feel sick | A kind of tax
